### Disturbances of the Self

- **Aspects of the experience of the self:**
  - Awareness of the body (distinct from body image)
  - Awareness of the unity between various aspects of the self
  - Recognition of activities and thoughts as our own
  - Recognition of boundary between self and the outside world
  - Awareness of a continuity of past and present self
- **Disturbances concerned with activities:**
- **Disturbed awareness of the unity of the self:**
  - Autoscopic hallucinations in near-death experiences
  - Doppelgangers, where experiences two selves present at the same time, but w/ conviction that each is a version of the self
  - Dissociative identity disorders, where experience of two selves, but occuring at alternative times
- **Disturbances of the unity of the self:**
  - May be experienced as a different person from the one who existed before the disorder began
  - May be experienced as a different person has replaced the old self

